---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { site, toolkit } from '../data/site';
import Art from '../components/Art.astro';
const hasHeadshot = existsSync('public/headshot.png');
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <img class="hero-photo" src="/photos/hero.jpg" alt="" width="1792" height="768" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="hero-shade"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">DevOps · DevSecOps · AI governance</p>
        <h1>DevOps engineer building toward <em>AI governance</em>.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I build and run containerized, CI/CD-driven systems in regulated environments, with a growing
          focus on security, compliance, and how AI systems should be governed.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/projects">See projects</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="portrait">
        {hasHeadshot
          ? <img class="headshot" src="/headshot.png" alt={`Portrait of ${site.name}`} width="220" height="220" />
          : <div class="initials" aria-hidden="true">MC</div>}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The path</p>
      <h2>From pipelines to policy</h2>
      <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:24px">
        <article class="card">
          <Art kind="devops" class="icon" />
          <span class="step">01 · Foundation</span>
          <h3>DevOps</h3>
          <p>
            Containerization, CI/CD pipelines, and Python backend APIs, built in a regulated aerospace
            environment where pipelines have to satisfy compliance requirements as well as ship software.
            That discipline transfers directly to SaaS, healthcare, finance, and critical infrastructure.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <Art kind="security" class="icon" />
          <span class="step">02 · Growing</span>
          <h3>Security &amp; compliance</h3>
          <p>
            The newer part of my work: remediating container vulnerabilities with Trivy and contributing
            to NIST 800-171 and authorization-to-operate (ATO) compliance efforts. I'm building depth here
            deliberately; it's the bridge between the engineering I know and the governance work I'm heading toward.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <Art kind="governance" class="icon" />
          <span class="step">03 · Direction</span>
          <h3>AI governance &amp; policy</h3>
          <p>
            An MS in Management &amp; Policy (Translator track) at Purdue University, graduating after
            Spring 2027, and the AIGP certification in progress. The goal: roles where someone who knows
            how systems are actually built and deployed helps translate between engineering teams and
            policy requirements.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Toolkit</p>
      <h2>What I work with</h2>
      <dl class="toolkit">
        {toolkit.map((t) => (
          <div class="row">
            <dt>{t.group}</dt>
            <dd><ul class="tags">{t.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul></dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
        <h2>Translating between people and systems</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Much of my experience is in Behavior-Driven Development: working with stakeholders to turn
          expectations into testable, shared definitions of done before anything is built. It's the same
          skill a translator role needs, whether the gap is between product and engineering or between
          policy and implementation, and it's why I'm drawn toward business analysis and governance work
          alongside engineering.
        </p>
        <p>I'm a U.S. Navy veteran.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="callout">
        <img class="callout-photo" src="/photos/research.jpg" alt="" width="1536" height="640" loading="lazy" />
        <div class="callout-shade"></div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research interest</p>
        <h2>AI and under-catalogued historical sources</h2>
        <p>
          I'm interested in applying AI tooling to under-catalogued Austronesian and Philippine historical
          sources, including manuscript digitization. Questions of data sovereignty and research ethics are
          concrete there rather than abstract, which makes it a useful lens on AI governance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
